  "sources": {
    "ultimate": "IS 456 38.1: εcu 0.0035, the parabola-rectangle 0.67 fck/γm to 0.002, γm 1.5 (36.4.2), steel fy/1.15; the rectangular block here is the one with the same force and centroid, 0.36 fck xu at 0.42 xu (Annex G): η = 0.36/(0.84 × 0.4467), λ = 0.84 (SAEngine form of IS's block)",
    "ultimate.relations": "Ec = 5000 √fck (6.2.3.1), fcr = 0.7 √fck (6.2.2); the high-strength relations of the generic form are not used by IS (highFrom 100 MPa)",
    "ultimate.axialShares": "IS 456 39.3: Pu = 0.4 fck Ac + 0.67 fy Asc (with emin ≤ 0.05 D), taken as the cap of the interaction surface (SAEngine practice, on the safe side with the minimum eccentricity also applied)",
    "ultimate.eccentricity": "IS 456 25.4: emin = l/500 + D/30 >= 20 mm",
    "shear": "IS 456 Table 19 (τc by pt and grade), Table 20 (τc,max), 40.4 (Vus = 0.87 fy Asv d/sv), 26.5.1.6 (Asv/(b sv) >= 0.4/(0.87 fy)), 26.5.1.5 (sv <= 0.75 d, 300 mm), 40.2.1.1 (k of slabs)",
    "torsion": "IS 456 41.3.1 (Ve = Vu + 1.6 T/b), 41.4.2 (Mt = T(1 + D/b)/1.7), 41.4.3 (Asv), 26.5.1.7 (spacing x1, (x1 + y1)/4, 300 mm)",
    "punching": "IS 456 31.6.1 (d/2), 31.6.3.1 (ks τc, ks = 0.5 + βc <= 1, τc = 0.25 √fck), 31.6.3.2 (1.5 τc with shear reinforcement, 0.5 Vc)",
    "deflection": "IS 456 23.2.1 (7, 20, 26; × 10/span beyond 10 m), Figures 4-6 (the tension curve as the usual fit), 23.2(a) span/250, (b) span/350 or 20 mm; Annex C: Ieff C-2.1, shrinkage C-3 (k3, k4, εcs 0.0003 by 6.2.4.1), creep C-4 with θ of 6.2.5.1 (7 days 2.2, 28 days 1.6, 1 year 1.1)",
    "cracking": "IS 456 35.3.2 (0.3 mm; 0.004 × cover, taken as the 0.1-0.2 mm values here for aggressive conditions: SAEngine reading), Annex F (Wcr formula); tanks IS 3370 (Part 2):2009 0.2 mm",
    "cover": "IS 456 Table 16 (20, 30, 45, 50, 75 mm), notes 1-2 (5 mm less for bars up to 12 mm in mild; 5 mm less at M35 and above in severe and very severe), 26.4.2.1 (columns 40 mm), 26.4.2.2 (footings 50 mm)",
    "durability": "IS 456 Table 5 (reinforced concrete: least cement 300/300/320/340/360 kg/m³, largest free w/c 0.55/0.50/0.45/0.45/0.40, least grade M20/M25/M30/M35/M40)",
    "anchorage": "IS 456 26.2.1 (Ld = φ σs/(4 τbd)), 26.2.1.1 (τbd 1.0-1.9 for M15-M40, + 60 % deformed bars, + 25 % compression), 26.2.5.1 (laps: Ld or 30 φ flexural tension, 2 Ld or 30 φ direct tension, Ld or 24 φ compression; no laps above 36 mm)",
    "memberLimits": "IS 456 26.5.1.1 (0.85/fy, 0.04 b D), 26.5.1.3 (side face 0.1 %, D > 750 mm), 26.5.2.1 (0.12 % / 0.15 %), 26.5.2.2 (D/8), 26.3.3 (3 d or 300 mm; 5 d or 450 mm), 26.5.3.1 (0.8-6 %, 4 and 6 bars, 12 mm), 26.5.3.2 (ties φ/4 and 6 mm, pitch min(least dimension, 16 φ, 300 mm))",
    "columns": "IS 456 25.1.2 (lex/D > 12 slender), 25.3.1 (60), 39.7.1 (Pu D/2000 (lex/D)²), 39.7.1.1 (k), 39.6 (αn 1.0 to 2.0 from Pu/Puz 0.2 to 0.8, Puz = 0.45 fck Ac + 0.75 fy Asc)",
    "twoWaySlabs": "IS 456 Annex D Table 26 (restrained panels, nine cases), Table 27 (simply supported), D-1.1 (middle strip 3/4), D-1.8 (corner steel 3/4 over lx/5, half with one edge continuous)",
    "flatSlabs": "IS 456 31.4.3.3 (end span by αc), 31.5.5 (column strip 75 %, 100 %, 60 %), 31.2.1 (125 mm)",
    "walls": "IS 456 32.2.5 (Puw = 0.3 (t - 1.2 e - 2 ea) fck Lw, ea = Hwe²/2500 t), 32.2.3 (Hwe/t <= 30), 32.4.2-32.4.4 (shear), 32.5 (steel 0.0012/0.0015 vertical, 0.0020/0.0025 horizontal, 3 t and 450 mm)",
    "footings": "IS 456 34.1.2 (150 mm on soil, 300 mm on piles), 34.4 (0.45 fck √(A1/A2), the root at most 2)",
    "shear.axialFactor": "IS 456 40.2.2: members under axial compression, τc × δ, δ = 1 + 3 Pu/(Ag fck) <= 1.5; under net tension SAEngine continues the line, not below 0 (no IS rule; on the safe side)",
    "shear.enhancement": "IS 456 40.5.1: τc × 2 d / av within 2 d of a support (used for corbels); 40.5.2: beams carrying distributed loads checked at d from the face (SAEngine's checks do so), the enhancement not taken for beams (on the safe side)",
    "deepBeams": "IS 456 29.1 (deep when l/D < 2.0 simply supported, < 2.5 continuous; l the lesser of c/c and 1.15 clear span), 29.2 (z = 0.2 (l + 2D) for 1 <= l/D <= 2, 0.6 l below 1, simply supported; 0.2 (l + 1.5 D) for 1 <= l/D <= 2.5, 0.5 l below 1, continuous), 29.3.1 (tension bars within 0.25 D - 0.05 l of the tension face), 29.3.4 (side face steel as the least steel of walls, 32.5); the hogging steel zones of 29.3.2 are not checked",
    "corbels": "IS 456 28.1 (av < d; outer edge at least half the depth at the face), 28.2.1-28.2.3 (the tie at the root; horizontal force resisted at least 0.5 Vu), 28.2.2 with 34.4 (bearing 0.45 fck), 28.2.4 (shear at the face by 40 with the enhancement of 40.5; horizontal links in the upper 2/3 d at least half the main tension steel)",
    "walls.axial": "IS 456 32.2.5 (Puw = 0.3 (t - 1.2 e - 2 ea) fck Lw, e >= t/20, ea = Hwe²/(2500 t)), 32.2.3-32.2.4 (Hwe/t <= 30; Hwe 0.75 H braced and restrained, 1.0 H braced, 2.0 H unbraced: SAEngine's bracing flags)",
    "twoWaySlabs.corner": "IS 456 D-1.8 (both edges discontinuous: top and bottom meshes each way of 3/4 of the largest midspan steel over lx/5), D-1.9 (one edge continuous: half of that), D-1.10 (both continuous: none)",
    "seismic": "IS 13920:2016: beams 6.1-6.3, columns 7.1-7.3 (7.2.1 strong column 1.4), special confining reinforcement 8, joints 9, special shear walls 10 (boundary elements 10.4, coupling beams 10.5)"
  }
